/**
 * Golden binding corpus: what the legacy binding kinds resolve to, pinned.
 *
 * The cases were recorded from server/automation/bind.js BEFORE its code moved
 * into this directory (legacy.mjs, resolve.mjs), so they are today's runtime
 * behaviour, not a second, independently invented truth. They cover every
 * dialect a stored automation can hold: canonical paths, `[0]` and `.0`,
 * nested `[*]`, quoted and hyphenated keys, `trigger.x` without `.output`,
 * missing values, null rows, JSON templates, listAsMarkdown,
 * leaveUnresolved, the gallery templates (server/automation/templates.js) and
 * the paths the AI builder's normaliser writes.
 *
 * Some expectations are WRONG on purpose: `steps.s1.output.items.0.subject`
 * is undefined and `{{vars.objs}}` renders as JSON. That is what a stored
 * automation does today, and backward compatibility means it keeps doing so
 * until a milestone changes it deliberately and updates the case here.
 *
 * The same file runs under node --test (server), vitest (agent-hub, the
 * generated copy) and jest (mobile, the vendored copy), so the preview on the
 * web and on the phone equals the run. Add a case HERE, never in one runner.
 * Every case runs against a FRESH makeState(): interpolateTemplate pushes onto
 * `_templateWarnings`, and a shared object would leak between cases.
 */

